# expected_value.fw — expectation E[X] as a Sigma value*probability sum.
#
# The general definition of the expected value of a discrete random variable is
#
#   E[X] = sum over outcomes of  value * probability
#
# expressed directly as a bounded aggregation (the Sigma form). This file gives
# the discrete-UNIFORM case over {1..N}: every value v in [1..N] has equal
# probability 1/N, so
#
#   expected_value(N) = sum(v * (1/N), v in [1..N]) = (N+1)/2
#
# For a fair N-sided die this is the mean pip value: expected_value(6) = 3.5.
#
# General (non-uniform) expectations follow the same Sigma value*prob shape with
# the value/probability written as expressions of the iterator; see
# order_statistic.fw and the PNF card-deck E[max] dogfood for a non-uniform
# example built from this primitive.
#
# NOTE: the iterator is named v, NOT i — i is the built-in imaginary unit and the
# rewrite rule i^2 = -1 would corrupt any squared-iterator body before the
# aggregation unrolls.
#
# NOTE: the function name matches the filename (expected_value) — cross-file
# named-call dispatch resolves a section call by filename.
#
# Usage:
#   expected_value(N=6, result=?m)          # mean of a fair 6-sided die -> 3.5

[expected_value(N) -> result]
result = sum(v * (1/N), v in [1..N])
